I have found the tag-overflow / "+N" utility. Here is the complete picture.

## 1. Source implementation file paths

There are two layers to this feature in the `/app` monorepo:

**Core layout logic (framework-agnostic utility):**
- `/app/packages/utilities/src/overflowHandler/overflowHandler.ts`

**React hook (the version that actually feeds the "+N" tag renderer):**
- `/app/packages/react/src/internal/useOverflowItems.ts`

**The consumer that renders the actual "+N" overflow pill:**
- `/app/packages/react/src/components/PageHeader/PageHeader.tsx` (the `PageHeaderTabBar` sub-component)

## 2. Relevant code excerpts

### a) Core `overflowHandler.ts` — the fit/overflow decision (`updateOverflowHandler`)

This function decides how many items are visible vs. hidden, honoring `maxVisibleItems`, and toggles a `data-offset` element (the container that holds the overflow indicator/popover). Key logic (lines 67–123):

```ts
const totalSize = sizes.reduce((sum, size) => sum + size, 0);
const totalFixedSize = fixedSizes.reduce((sum, size) => sum + size, 0);

if (totalSize + totalFixedSize <= containerSize) {
  visibleItems = maxVisibleItems ? items.slice(0, maxVisibleItems) : [...items];
  hiddenItems  = maxVisibleItems ? items.slice(maxVisibleItems)   : [];
} else {
  const available = containerSize - offsetSize;   // reserve room for the "+N" offset element
  let accumulated = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {
    const size = sizes[i];
    if (accumulated + size + totalFixedSize <= available) {
      visibleItems.push(items[i]);
      accumulated += size;
    } else {
      hiddenItems.push(items[i]);
    }
  }
}
...
visibleItems.forEach((item) => item.removeAttribute('data-hidden'));
hiddenItems.forEach((item) => item.setAttribute('data-hidden', ''));
if (offset) {
  offset.toggleAttribute('data-hidden', hiddenItems.length !== 0); // show offset only when something overflows
}
onChange(visibleItems, hiddenItems);
```

`maxVisibleItems` is defined on both `UpdateOverflowHandlerOptions` (line 52) and `OverflowHandlerOptions` (line 136), and validated in `createOverflowHandler` (lines 172–177: must be a positive integer). `createOverflowHandler` (lines 159–221) wires this up with a `ResizeObserver`, and identifies the offset element via the `data-offset` attribute (line 182) and fixed items via `data-fixed` (line 183). Note: this core utility does not itself print "+N" — it exposes visible/hidden arrays via `onChange` and toggles the offset element; the consumer renders the count.

### b) React hook `useOverflowItems.ts` — computes visible items, hidden items and the count

The `getVisibleItems` reducer applies `maxItems` first, then measures accumulated width against available `maxWidth` (container width minus the offset/"more" element width). Lines 46–119:

```ts
const handleResize = () => {
  if (containerRef.current) {
    const offset = offsetRef?.current?.offsetWidth || 0;
    const newMax = containerRef.current.offsetWidth - offset;   // reserve space for offset ("+N")
    setMaxWidth(newMax);
  }
};
...
const visibleItems = overflowItems
  .slice(0, maxItems)                       // maxItems applied here
  .reduce((prev, cur) => {
    if (maxReached) return prev;
    const itemWidth = map.get(cur.id) || 0;
    const willFit = accumulatedWidth + itemWidth <= maxWidth;
    if (willFit) { accumulatedWidth += itemWidth; prev.push(cur); }
    else { maxReached = true; }
    return prev;
  }, [] as T[]);
...
const hiddenItems = useMemo(
  () => overflowItems.slice(visibleItems.length),  // everything that didn't fit
  [overflowItems, visibleItems]
);
```

The "+N" count is simply `hiddenItems.length`.

### c) `PageHeader.tsx` (`PageHeaderTabBar`) — renders the tag row and the "+N" pill

Lines 632–688. It calls the hook and renders visible `Tag`s, then an `OperationalTag` whose text is the overflow count, with the hidden tags inside a `Popover`:

```tsx
const { visibleItems = [], hiddenItems = [], itemRefHandler = () => {} } =
  useOverflowItems<TagItem>(
    tagsWithIds,
    tagsContainerRef as React.RefObject<HTMLDivElement>,
    offsetRef as React.RefObject<HTMLDivElement>
  ) || { visibleItems: [], hiddenItems: [], itemRefHandler: () => {} };
...
{visibleItems.map((tag) => (
  <Tag key={tag.id} ref={(node) => itemRefHandler(tag.id, node)} type={tag.type} size={tag.size} ...>
    {tag.text}
  </Tag>
))}

{hiddenItems.length > 0 && (
  <Popover open={openPopover} onRequestClose={() => setOpenPopover(false)}>
    <OperationalTag
      onClick={handleOverflowClick}
      aria-expanded={openPopover}
      text={`+${hiddenItems.length}`}      // <-- the "+N" overflow indicator pill
      size={tagSize}
    />
    <PopoverContent className="tag-popover-content">
      <div className={`${prefix}--page-header__tags-popover-list`}>
        {hiddenItems.map((tag) => (
          <Tag key={tag.id} type={tag.type} size={tag.size}>{tag.text}</Tag>
        ))}
      </div>
    </PopoverContent>
  </Popover>
)}
```

## 3. Related tests, demos, and docs

**Tests:**
- `/app/packages/utilities/src/overflowHandler/overflowHandler-test.js` — tests the core utility (including `maxVisibleItems` behavior).
- `/app/packages/react/src/internal/__tests__/useOverflowItems-test.js` — tests the React hook.
- `/app/packages/react/src/components/PageHeader/PageHeader-test.js` — mocks both `useOverflowItems` and `createOverflowHandler` (see lines 32–54) and drives `mockOverflowOnChange` to test the tag overflow rendering.

**Docs / README:**
- `/app/packages/utilities/src/overflowHandler/README.md` — documents `createOverflowHandler`, `maxVisibleItems`, and the `data-hidden` / `data-fixed` / `data-offset` attributes, with a Lit usage example.
- `/app/packages/utilities/src/overflowHandler/index.ts` and `/app/packages/utilities/src/index.ts` — export the utility publicly (as `@carbon/utilities`).

**Demo / story pages:**
- `/app/packages/react/src/components/PageHeader/PageHeader.stories.js` — NOTE: this is now only a deprecation stub. The `Default` export (lines 26–38) just says `PageHeader` has moved from `@carbon/react` to `@carbon/ibm-products` (issue #21926), so the live tag-overflow demo now lives in the ibm-products repo, not here. The rendering code (`PageHeader.tsx`) is still present in this repo.

**Not related (despite name matches):** The `overflow-menu` components in `/app/packages/web-components/src/components/overflow-menu/` and `/app/packages/react/src/components/OverflowMenu*` are a different feature (a "..." dropdown menu), not the tag "+N" overflow layout. `breadcrumb-item.ts` in web-components also references `maxVisibleItems` for breadcrumb overflow, which is a separate consumer of the same concept but not tag-specific.

### Summary
The overflow layout algorithm lives in two places: the framework-agnostic `overflowHandler.ts` (`updateOverflowHandler`) and the React `useOverflowItems.ts` hook. Both compute which items fit (accumulating widths against container width minus an offset), apply `maxVisibleItems`/`maxItems`, and expose `visibleItems`/`hiddenItems`. The actual "+N" pill is produced by the consumer `PageHeaderTabBar` in `PageHeader.tsx` via `text={`+${hiddenItems.length}`}` on an `OperationalTag`.
